This actually links to a big design issue: how do we arrange the code in a
way we can use that from different packages? Fr the moment the solution is
that we give a symlink to the "common" code in the repo. At the
distrib-build stage, we check the code out (so by following the link the
"shared" code is exported rom single location), and build the package.

In a regular world one would use libraries for such situation. But we are
in the R world.  A UseR! this summer I was talking to Hadley Wickham, and
he was sure the solution is possible.

Y

